{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "0BX4", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-valuative-criteria}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ffb871818bbeb4ece17589d8533c873099e5f24d39c4e1fde9fc9f5cd03424d7", "source_text": "Valuative criteria", "source_text_hash": "sha256:f2781c15b264ed3651ad8d8a44525e33a5da53eca84c4df4bf4af418cea98d0e", "unit_id": "tag:0BX4:title"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0BX4", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-section-valuative-criterion-universal-closedness}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-section-valuative-separatedness}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{limits-section-Noetherian-valuative-criterion}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d401402851174c80c38a7a188917cfb992fead7264d4c42097629159aee60932", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nWe have already discussed the valuative criterion for universal closedness\nand for separatedness in Schemes, Sections\n<REF_0001> and\n<REF_0002>.\nIn this section we will discuss some consequences and variants.\nIn Limits, Section <REF_0003>\nwe will show that it suffices to consider discrete valuation\nrings when working with locally Noetherian schemes and\nmorphisms of finite type.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d5b9ee1b69320e54d81f01ef6c2da0153caef9822304726cb9b47145f943a181", "unit_id": "tag:0BX4:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0BX4", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{reference}\n\\cite[II Theorem 7.3.8]{EGA}\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$S$", "MATH_0002": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$f$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\Spec(K) \\ar[r] \\ar[d] & X \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\Spec(A) \\ar[r] \\ar@{-->}[ru] & Y\n}\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$A$", "MATH_0009": "$K$", "OWNARGEND_0001": "]\n\\label{lemma-characterize-proper}\n", "REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-definition-valuative-criterion}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}[", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:537385d24c9362169919ee849c1184f46b16e4b3155f7b5bbfd002e54e98c4c5", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2fe6874c2e07d30a64987b964a62f6a6011e1bab6e89e03015beeb6c92e2005c", "source_text": "Valuative criterion for properness<OWNARGEND_0001><LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Let <MATH_0002> be a morphism of schemes\nover <MATH_0003>. Assume <MATH_0004> is of finite type and quasi-separated.\nThen the following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0005> is proper,\n<STRUCT_0003> <MATH_0006> satisfies the valuative criterion\n(Schemes, Definition <REF_0001>),\n<STRUCT_0004> given any commutative solid diagram\n<MATH_0007>\nwhere <MATH_0008> is a valuation ring with field of fractions <MATH_0009>, there exists\na unique dotted arrow making the diagram commute.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3660ba46c1fdb08373240c2dd3400e68793df544830cabaddb1c7132716a4c50", "unit_id": "tag:0BX5:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0BX4", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{schemes-proposition-characterize-universally-closed}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-separated-implies-valuative}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{schemes-lemma-valuative-criterion-separatedness}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:eb7cb5dbce6e8c6fbf9aafd694d14a4b3beac1ddb560447368eab4856bdbd14f", "source_text": "Part (3) is a reformulation of (2). Thus the lemma is a formal\nconsequence of\nSchemes, Proposition <REF_0001>\nand Lemma <REF_0002>,\nLemma <REF_0003>,\nand the definitions.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:44b4f87250061df4ff87e468fb284941eee5e690b0ea1a724f83e6f4bb54a403", "unit_id": "tag:0BX5:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0BX4", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7ef2d2fb6ca3326ee34dc8c717c49aa29b925747667e20211a641c872306bb4c", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nOne usually does not have to consider all possible diagrams\nwhen testing the valuative criterion. We will call a valuative\ncriterion as in the next lemma a ``refined valuative criterion''.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:56031d5c4b2e9e02e9640538cbff4fea6bba04e4d99572672d42f6bcd331038e", "unit_id": "tag:0BX4:prose-0002"}
